{
  "duration": 43.479,
  "phrases": [
    {
      "start": 0.099,
      "end": 0.979,
      "text": "So welcome back again."
    },
    {
      "start": 1.5,
      "end": 4.38,
      "text": "It's time to solve one more problem. Now in this problem, we are given that"
    },
    {
      "start": 4.88,
      "end": 7.179,
      "text": "cos of A is equal to five by 13."
    },
    {
      "start": 7.639,
      "end": 9.42,
      "text": "The question is asking us to find sine of"
    },
    {
      "start": 9.84,
      "end": 10.899,
      "text": "90 degrees minus A."
    },
    {
      "start": 11.34,
      "end": 13.019,
      "text": "This is a direct identity question."
    },
    {
      "start": 13.479,
      "end": 15.039,
      "text": "We do not need to make a triangle here."
    },
    {
      "start": 15.339,
      "end": 18.68,
      "text": "We only need to remember one co-function identity."
    },
    {
      "start": 19.319,
      "end": 21.299,
      "text": "The identity is sine of"
    },
    {
      "start": 21.6,
      "end": 22.919,
      "text": "90 degree minus theta"
    },
    {
      "start": 23.399,
      "end": 25.219,
      "text": "is equal to cos of theta."
    },
    {
      "start": 25.599,
      "end": 31.76,
      "text": "So if theta is A, then we can write sine of 90 degree minus A is equal to cos of A. And cos of A is already given as"
    },
    {
      "start": 32.2,
      "end": 33.219,
      "text": "five by 13."
    },
    {
      "start": 33.619,
      "end": 34.479,
      "text": "So directly sine of"
    },
    {
      "start": 34.779,
      "end": 37.399,
      "text": "90 degree minus A is equal to five by 13."
    },
    {
      "start": 37.86,
      "end": 38.239,
      "text": "Hence,"
    },
    {
      "start": 38.559,
      "end": 39.419,
      "text": "the final answer is"
    },
    {
      "start": 39.819,
      "end": 40.799,
      "text": "five by 13."
    },
    {
      "start": 41.2,
      "end": 43.479,
      "text": "So the correct option is option B."
    }
  ],
